<header><p class="enc-kicker">Work / monument</p><h1 class="enc-title">Linux</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1991">1991</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Linux is a family of free and open-source operating systems built on the Linux kernel, first released in 1991 by the Finnish student <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/linus-torvalds">Linus Torvalds</a>. Developed collaboratively over the internet and usually combined with GNU software, it became the dominant system on web servers and supercomputers and underlies the Android mobile operating system, making it one of the most widely used pieces of software in the world.</p></div>
